Hello Argonauts and other interested parties,

I would like to announce my candidacy for PTL of the Cinder project for
the 2027.1 (Indri) cycle.

I've served as PTL before, so I know what I'm getting into.  In the time
since the Yoga cycle, which was my last term as PTL, I served on the
OpenStack Technical Committee for two years (2022-2023).  This broadened
my perspective on how the various OpenStack projects hang together.
More recently, I've been serving on the Vulnerability Management Team,
which has been an eye-opening experience.  I've also continued to serve
as a Cinder core reviewer, and I'm sure that many of you have seen my
comments on your patches.

Under Jon's leadership over the past five cycles, the Cinder project is
in a good place, with some new cinder cores and other enthusiastic
contributors joining the project.  My primary concern over the next
cycle is to improve the security stance of the cinder volume and backup
drivers; other project goals will be determined by the consensus of the
Cinder community (there are currently several initiatives working their
way through the specs process).

I intend to continue the popular Festival of Reviews and video mid-cycle
meetings, as these seem important in keeping the project moving.

Thank you for your consideration of my candidacy.

Brian Rosmaita (rosmaita)



